#8 7.529 Repository: 'deb https://ppa.launchpadcontent.net/deadsnakes/ppa/ubuntu/ jammy main'
#8 7.529 Description:
#8 7.529 This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Update Note
#8 7.529 ===========
#8 7.529 Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Reporting Issues
#8 7.529 ================
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
#8 7.529 https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
#8 7.529 ====================================
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
#8 7.529 - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
#8 7.529 - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
#8 7.529 - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Why some packages aren't built:
#8 7.529 - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
#8 7.529 - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Packages
#8 7.529 ========
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
#8 7.529 - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
#8 7.529 - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
#8 7.529 - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
#8 7.529 - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
#8 7.529 - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Third-Party Python Modules
#8 7.529 ==========================
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
#8 7.529 https://packaging.python.org/installing/
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Sources
#8 7.529 =======
#8 7.529 The package sources are available at:
#8 7.529 https://github.com/deadsnakes/
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 Nightly Builds
#8 7.529 ==============
#8 7.529 
#8 7.529 For nightly builds, see ppa:deadsnakes/nightly https://launchpad.net/~deadsnakes/+archive/ubuntu/nightly
#8 7.529 More info: https://launchpad.net/~deadsnakes/+archive/ubuntu/ppa
